    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0576" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.38/54.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-29T18:00:00-04:49">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 29, 1915—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Having received the invitation of the Haitian Government to enter into modus
                    vivendi, I accepted, stating my readiness to enter into modus vivendi embodyng
                    the same terms as the treaty. After numerous conferences the following modus
                    vivendi was agreed upon and in accordance with your instructions was signed
                    today at 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>[Here follows the modus vivendi, identical with the inclosures with Mr.
                    Blanchard’s No. 51 of December 6; see post.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
